      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224552/assets/f9f59d4328ad43e6e342da3cf9e87ccd5dfe33b97c46424e7fcc2b9f562fc452.png)\n\nFind the tangent of $∠N.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the definition of tangent: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡N=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{OM}{MN}=\\frac{OM}{2.5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $OM.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}OM & =\\sqrt{O{N}^{2}-M{N}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6.5}^{2}-{2.5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{42.25-6.25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡N & =\\frac{OM}{2.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
